-- title:
--   Regular parameter with residually characteristic-zero quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a type carrying the structure of a commutative ring which is an integral domain, which is a regular local ring and a regular ring, and whose characteristic is zero (so that $\mathbb{Z} \to R$ is injective). Assume moreover that the Krull dimension of $R$, in the form `ringKrullDim R` valued in $\mathbb{Z}$ extended by $\pm\infty$, satisfies $2 \le \dim R$. The assertion is that there exists an element $x \in R$ with four properties: $x$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $R$ (the maximal ideal of the local ring, `maximalIdeal R`); $x$ does not lie in $\mathfrak m^2$, so that $x$ is part of a regular system of parameters; $x \ne 0$; and the quotient ring $R/(x)$ by the ideal generated by the single element $x$ is again of characteristic zero, i.e. the natural map $\mathbb{Z} \to R/(x)$ is injective.
--
--   This is the standard prime-avoidance construction of a regular parameter that may be cut out without introducing torsion: in a regular local domain of characteristic zero and dimension at least two one can choose $x \in \mathfrak m \setminus \mathfrak m^2$ so that $R/(x)$ is still of characteristic zero (and is a domain). It is used in the construction of a discrete valuation ring mapping to a regular local ring of dimension at most two that is adically complete with $n \ne 0$ for natural numbers $n$, namely in [`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_ringHom_comp_eq_of_ringKrullDim_le_two_of_isAdicComplete_of_natCast_ne_zero`](thm.html#IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_ringHom_comp_eq_of_ringKrullDim_le_two_of_isAdicComplete_of_natCast_ne_zero).
-- source:
